AB  - The increasing demand for emotionally supportive dialogue systems underscores the need for models that not only exhibit empathy but also reason about the underlying causes of users' emotions. However, existing conversational AI models often fall short in generating responses that are both emotionally resonant and contextually grounded. To address this challenge, we propose CES-CoT (Cause-aware Emotion-focused and Strategy-driven Chain-of-Thought), a novel framework that integrates structured emotional reasoning into large language models (LLMs). CES-CoT decomposes the generation process into interpretable reasoning steps involving emotion identification, causal attribution, stimulus extraction, individual appraisal, and support strategy justification. This enables the model to generate responses that are not only empathetic but also causally transparent and strategically aligned. To support the framework, we construct CESD-CoT, a high-quality dataset containing cause-aware emotional support dialogues with detailed chain-of-thought annotations. We fine-tune multiple LLMs under the CES-CoT paradigm and evaluate them on both automatic and human-centric metrics. Experimental results show substantial improvements in empathy, coherence, and interpretability over existing baselines (1).
