AB  - Emotional support chatbots are becoming increasingly important as they can understand and potentially support people's emotional health. This study focuses on developing text-based, lightweight plug-and-play models for emotion recognition using machine learning (ML) and natural language processing (NLP), which are an essential component of emotional support chatbots. Our experiments show that the DistilBERT model is able to detect emotions in conversations faster and with comparable accuracy to other state-of-the-art methods. Our implementation of a Streamlit APP visualizes the emotion recognition results for an input utterance. This facilitates the application of the language model in a real chatbot as a virtual companion for active assisted living (AAL) for older people.
