TI  - Ethical and Empathetic Requirements for Trustworthy ChatBots
T2  - 2025 IEEE 33RD INTERNATIONAL REQUIREMENTS ENGINEERING CONFERENCE WORKSHOPS, REW
LA  - English
CP  - 33rd International Requirements Engineering Conference-RE-Annual
AB  - As large language model (LLM)-based chatbots become prevalent across domains such as healthcare, education, and customer service, ensuring their behavior aligns with normative requirements (NR) becomes essential for fostering trust in these systems. Yet, eliciting these requirements for such LLM-based chatbots remains challenging, due to their open-ended capabilities. In this paper, we propose NR that describe how chatbot responses should behave to be compliant with the norms, across varying inputs, contexts, and user profiles in three application domains: therapy, education, and customer service.
