TI  - KidMind: An open framework to develop and benchmark LLMs for empathetic companionship and knowledge reasoning in Chinese child mental health support
T2  - KNOWLEDGE-BASED SYSTEMS
LA  - English
KW  - Child psychology
KW  - Large language model
KW  - Dataset&benchmark
KW  - Open leaderboard
AB  - Children face growing mental health challenges, creating opportunities for LLM-based psychological support. Yet existing psychological LLMs, primarily trained on adult data, are poorly aligned with children's linguistic, cognitive, and emotional characteristics. To address this gap, we introduce KidMind, a pioneering open and extensible framework for Chinese child mental health support that integrates KidIns, KidGPT, and KidBen into a unified ecosystem spanning data construction, model development, and fine-grained assessment. To address the scarcity of child counseling data due to privacy concerns, we develop KidIns, a 33.7k instruction dataset built from real-world resources using LLM-augmented methods, designed to reflect the linguistic and cultural characteristics of Chinese children. Quality assessments confirm its high acceptability and natural child-language alignment. Leveraging KidIns, we fine-tune the Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct base LLM to create KidGPT, a child-oriented LLM for empathetic companionship and knowledge reasoning. KidBen, our new benchmark, uses GPT-4.1 as a simulated human judge to jointly evaluate context-aware multi-turn response generation and child-psychology knowledge through expanded tasks and detailed metrics. Evaluations across 20 leading general and psychological LLMs show that KidGPT surpasses all baseline models by 23.39% and exhibits strong generalization capabilities, despite its compact parameter size. KidMind presents the research community with an opportunity to innovate AI technologies that benefit mental well-being. Our resources are available at https://github.com/wtiantianw/KidMind.
