KW  - LIVING ARRANGEMENTS
KW  - OLDER-ADULTS
KW  - ASSOCIATION
AB  - South Korea has recently been experiencing a rapid increase in marginalized populations, leading to a growing demand for accessible emotional care. We introduce OSED-Ko, the first large-scale Open-Source Empathy-Driven dialogue dataset in Korean, designed to post-train LLMs for empathetically engaging conversations across demographic groups. OSED-Ko employs multi-step prompting to augment seed datasets with diverse life experiences and Korean-specific sociolinguistic features while avoiding anthropomorphism, annotated with speaker role, age group, and gender. Human evaluation shows that LLMs fine-tuned with OSED-Ko substantially outperform vanilla baselines, with overall scores improving by +0.87 to +0.94 points across the two backbone models and empathy and coherence increasing by more than +1.0 on a 0-3 scale. Distinct-2 and Distinct-3 scores improve by +0.03 to +0.11 over vanilla models. Expert evaluation by two certified psychological counselors further shows that fine-tuning reduces anthropomorphism by more than 1.2 points and lowers toxicity to below 0.35 on a 0-3 scale. We anticipate that OSED-Ko will serve as a valuable resource for training models that support home-based emotional care services.
