AB  - The integration of artificial intelligence (AI) into psychotherapy presents dramatic possible evolutions with profound implications for clinical psychology and the delivery of therapeutic interventions. AI holds the possibility to enhance numerous aspects of psychotherapy via various routes (e.g., chatbots, personalized treatment plans, enhanced tracking and monitoring). Thus, it is essential to examine the compatibility and opportunities presented by widely used, empirically supported treatments such as Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT). The possibilities of advancement hold promise for optimizing outcomes, increasing accessibility, and addressing the evolving needs of both patients and providers. Despite the possibilities of advancement, this integration presents various challenges, including concerns regarding acceptability, ethical integrity, and potential impacts on processes such as the therapeutic alliance and diagnostic accuracy.
