AB  - Emotional Support Conversation (ESC) aims to ease a helpseeker' psychological distress through dialogue with a supporter. We propose CasDecNet (Cascading Fusion-Guided Decoding Network), a novel response generation model that enhances empathy in three stages: understanding context, acquiring cognitive and affective empathy, and incorporating strategic support. Our model uses multi-dimensional external knowledge to better infer the user's situation and implement empathy effectively. Experiments on the ESConv dataset show that CasDecNet outperforms baselines in both automatic and LLM-based evaluations, especially in terms of response diversity and empathy, indicating its promise for human-like emotional support.
