CP  - 2025 International Conference on Systems Man and Cybernetics-SMC-Annual-Navigating Frontiers: Smart Systems for a Dynamic World
KW  - Supportive Psychotherapy
KW  - Large Language Models
KW  - Supportive Dialogue
KW  - Doctor-Patient Communication
AB  - Medical disputes are often rooted in inadequate communication and poor service attitudes among healthcare providers, both of which can adversely affect the quality of care. Traditional communication training, typically centered on textbooks and mentorship from senior colleagues, may fall short in preparing professionals for real-world interactions. This study presents a psychological support training system powered by a reasoning-based large language model (LLM), offering a novel AI-driven approach to enhance communication skills. The system autonomously generates dynamic, context-rich virtual patient profiles that incorporate emotional states, medical conditions, and personal backgrounds. These profiles serve as the foundation for interactive training dialogues, with the model producing real-time, contextually appropriate responses based on user input. The system is designed to simulate realistic patient encounters, provide structured feedback through three performance indicators grounded in supportive psychotherapy, and enhance user motivation via supportive prompts and goal reminders. By enabling repeated reflection and fostering empathetic, professional communication, this text-based training tool offers an effective and scalable solution for improving the interpersonal competencies of healthcare practitioners, particularly those in the early stages of training.
